---
// Primer · For newcomers. Sets up *why* AI agents are needed for
// specialized scientific work before the rest of the landing page
// dives into AKD specifics. Sourced verbatim-ish from front.md and
// tightened for the page voice.
---
<section class="section section--primer" id="primer">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h1>Accelerated Knowledge Discovery: AI Agents for Science</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="primer-rows">
      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">01</span>
          <h3>The jagged edge of AI</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">Why generic chatbots fall short in science</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <p>Standard chatbots lack the specialized tools, databases, terminology, and ontologies that advanced science requires, so they hallucinate more often in narrow technical domains.</p>
          <p>Their value also depends on the user&rsquo;s expertise. A subject-matter expert can ask precise questions and judge weak reasoning; a novice may not know what to ask or how to verify a response.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">02</span>
          <h3>What are agents?</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">From responding to acting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <p>An AI agent is an independent digital worker. You give it a task and it figures out how to accomplish it.</p>
          <p>Unlike a chatbot that just responds, an agent analyzes the problem, breaks it into steps, uses the right tools, reviews results, and corrects mistakes along the way.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">03</span>
          <h3>What makes an agent well-designed</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">Reasoning · Context · Tools</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <ul class="primer-elements" aria-label="Three core elements of a well-designed agent">
            <li>
              <b>Reasoning logic</b>
              <span>Prompts or instructions that shape how the agent thinks through a task.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Contextual information</b>
              <span>Grounds the agent in the scientific domain it serves.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Tool access</b>
              <span>Clear guidance on which tool to use, when, and how.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="primer-row__caveat">Designed this way, the agent captures an expert&rsquo;s implicit knowledge so a novice can approach expert productivity.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section--primer {
    /* Compact landing-page section: title + three rows fit inside one
       viewport on a 1080p desktop. */
    padding: 36px 0 28px;
  }
  .section--primer .section-head {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .section--primer h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .primer-rows {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .primer-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }

  .primer-row__lead {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .primer-row__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .primer-row__lead h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .primer-row__hint {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .primer-row__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .primer-row__body p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .primer-row__body em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .primer-row__caveat {
    padding-left: 10px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-size: 12.5px !important;
  }

  /* Three-element list inside row 03: single-column inside the narrow card. */
  .primer-elements {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2px 0 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .primer-elements li {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
    padding: 2px 0 2px 10px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .primer-elements b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .primer-elements span {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .primer-rows { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
